# Functions

Functions are declared using the `func` keyword. Functions needs to declare all their arguments and return values types.
Like the Go programming language, types are declared after the name of the arguments.

In the example, `reshape` takes arguments `a` and `b` both of types `[2][3]float32` and return a single value of type `[3][2]float32`.


```code:main
package main

func addReshape(a, b [2][3]float32) [3][2]float32 {
    return [3][2]float32(a+b)
}

func Main() [3][2]float32 {
    a := [2][3]float32{{1, 2, 3}, {4, 5, 6}}
    b := -a
    return addReshape(a,b)
}
```

